nbecause it agrees with the restriction of\n<MATH_0045> on <MATH_0046>.\nMoreover, <MATH_0047> maps to the restriction of <MATH_0048>\nto <MATH_0049>.\n\n<STRUCT_0007><STRUCT_0008>\nSince <MATH_0050> is quasi-compact, there exists a finite list\nof elements <MATH_0051> such that\n<MATH_0052>, an integer <MATH_0053> and sections\n<MATH_0054> such that\n<MATH_0055> and <MATH_0056> maps to the section\n<MATH_0057> of <MATH_0058>.\nConsider the differences\n<MATH_0059>\nThese correspond to sections of <MATH_0060>\nover <MATH_0061> which are zero\non <MATH_0062>. In particular their images in\n<MATH_0063>\nare zero in <MATH_0064>.\nThus some high power of <MATH_0065> kills each and every one of these.\nIn other words, the elements <MATH_0066>, for some <MATH_0067>\nsatisfy the glueing condition of the sheaf property and\ngive rise to a section <MATH_0068> of <MATH_0069>\nover <MATH_0070> as desired.\n",
